This project is built on the engine of the NFS Underground 2 port (https://github.com/sanyokkua/nfsu2-xbox-port), which is
nfsu2-sw by antoxa2584x (Anton Artemov, https://github.com/antoxa2584x/nfsu2-sw) with the Apple host and Metal renderer of
nfsu2-ios by myUdav4iik (https://github.com/myUdav4iik/nfsu2-ios). Their files keep their authorship. How engine/ was made is
in docs/upstream-patches/, and this project's later changes are in its git history. Anyone reusing this project's code: keep
this credit, and the links to their projects, with it.

The facts about this game (addresses, the controller, save signing, the logo movies) were found first by HP-PS-Xbox-Recomp by
MiddleDucky (https://github.com/MiddleDucky/HP-PS-Xbox-Recomp, MIT, LICENSES/MIT-HP-PS-Xbox-Recomp.txt); the controller code
and the logo skip in engine/src/recomp_manual.c follow its code and say so where they do.
The Metal renderer's effects, pacing and resolution changes come from NFSU2Deadware by LeoDeadware
(https://github.com/LeoDeadware/NFSU2Deadware, MIT, LICENSES/MIT-NFSU2Deadware.txt); the installer's kit builder, build and
import scripts adapt its tools (MIT). xboxrecomp by sp00nz is MIT (LICENSES/MIT-xboxrecomp.txt); its APU and NV2A parts from
xemu are LGPL-2.1-or-later (LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-xemu.txt, LICENSES/NOTICE-xboxrecomp.txt): the installer ships them as object
files and links them on the player's Mac, so they can be relinked with modified versions. The settings menu follows the design
of SpeedBreaker's by project(u) (GPL-3.0-or-later) and draws with Dear ImGui (MIT, LICENSES/MIT-imgui.txt) in Roboto Medium
(Apache-2.0, LICENSES/Apache-2.0-Roboto.txt). Third-party libraries: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

No game code or data is part of this project or its releases: the game is built on the player's Mac from their own disc.
